# The JMdict archive CI validates against. EDRDG serves only a rolling
# JMdict.gz and edits senses in place, so pulling "current" on every run makes
# validation non-reproducible: an untouched entry goes red the week upstream
# revises its sense. CI therefore reads the exact archive named here, published
# as a release asset on this repository, and verifies its hash before use.
#
# Populated and advanced by the jmdict-pin workflow, which republishes the
# archive, refreshes the corpus fingerprints against it, and opens a PR with
# the result. Until it has run once, both values are empty and CI falls back to
# the rolling upstream download with a warning.
JMDICT_RELEASE_TAG=
JMDICT_SHA256=
